# FUSESAFE Material Selection

## 1. Selected Material

Material: Aluminium 2024-T3, bare sheet.

ANSYS Engineering Data name: `AA2024_T3_Bare_Provisional`

Status: PROVISIONAL educational modelling choice.

The material is modelled as homogeneous and isotropic for the current structural analysis.

## 2. Current ANSYS Material Properties

| Property | Value | Unit |
|---|---:|---|
| Young's modulus | 73100 | MPa |
| Poisson's ratio | 0.33 | Dimensionless |
| Tensile yield strength | 290 | MPa |
| Density | 2780 | kg/m³ |
| Bulk modulus | 71667 | MPa |
| Shear modulus | 27481 | MPa |

The 290 MPa yield-strength value is the current team-selected provisional FUSESAFE modelling input.

## 3. Historical Supplier Reference

An earlier material record used a typical tensile yield strength of 345 MPa from ASM MatWeb:

https://asm.matweb.com/search/SpecificMaterial.asp?bassnum=MA2024T3

An additional supplier reference is:

https://aerospacemetals.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/Aluminum-2024-T3.pdf

The 345 MPa value is retained as historical supplier reference data. It is not the current FUSESAFE ANSYS yield-strength input.

## 4. Yield Strength and Allowable Stress

For current FUSESAFE screening calculations, use:

Provisional yield strength = 290 MPa.

For required FoS = 2:

Allowable stress = 290 / 2 = 145 MPa.

This is a preliminary educational screening threshold, not a certified aircraft structural design allowable.

## 5. Limitations

The 290 MPa value has been selected by the FUSESAFE team for provisional modelling. It has not been established as the certified minimum yield strength for the exact sheet specification.

Before any real design application, confirm:

- Applicable material specification and temper.
- Bare or clad sheet condition.
- Product form and thickness range.
- Material direction and directional strength.
- Temperature applicability.
- Appropriate minimum design allowable.

Do not report a verified aircraft structural safety conclusion using these provisional properties.
